<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68308" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοιχός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>adulterer, paramour</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hippon.
				74
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				[1127.6]
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				168
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				191d
			</span></i>, etc.: prov., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύραν, δι᾽ ἧς γαλῆ καὶ μ. οὐκ
					εἰσέρχεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Apollod.Car.
					6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρκοι μοιχῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philonid.
					7
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκαρμένος μοιχὸν μιᾷ
			μαχαίρᾳ</span> having the head close shaven with a razor, as
			was done by way of punishment to persons taken in adultery, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				849
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
				<i>paramour</i>, of a sodomite, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1160.26
			</span></i><span class="entity">(iii/iv A. D.)</span>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμείχω</span>.) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>idolatrous person,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ep.Jac.
				4.4
			</span></i>.</div>
